# Testing Patterns

## Test Organization
- Place tests in `PetHoroscopeGenerator.Tests` project
- Use descriptive test class names (e.g., `MainLayoutTests`)
- Group related tests in the same class
- Use meaningful test method names

## Test Structure
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
- Use `[Fact]` for simple tests
- Use `[Theory]` with `[InlineData]` for parameterized tests
- Mock external dependencies

## Blazor Component Testing
- Test component rendering and behavior
- Verify event handling
- Test navigation and routing
- Mock injected services

## API Testing
- Test API client methods
- Mock HTTP responses
- Test error handling scenarios
- Verify caching behavior

## Example Test Pattern:
```csharp
[Fact]
public void Component_Renders_Correctly()
{
    // Arrange
    var component = RenderComponent<MyComponent>();
    
    // Act
    var element = component.Find(".my-class");
    
    // Assert
    Assert.NotNull(element);
    Assert.Equal("Expected Text", element.TextContent);
}
```

## Test Data
- Use realistic test data
- Create helper methods for common setup
- Use builders for complex objects
- Keep tests independent and isolated